{
  "id": "minimax-h3-10eros-beta5-turbo-pack",
  "name": "Community — MiniMax H3 (10Eros Max beta5, Turbo)",
  "version": "1.2.0",
  "author": "TenStrip",
  "nsfw": true,
  "description": "MiniMax H3 on TenStrip's 10Eros Max beta5 TURBO-hybrid: the same beta5 hybrid checkpoint with the turbo delta baked into the weights, so it runs at 8 steps with no Turbo LoRA to download or hold in memory (the author's figure: 4.2 GB saved against loading the LoRAs). One 21 GB INT8 file carries first-frame and reference-to-video character, so text-, image- and reference-to-video all run on it. Two-seed bake-off on a 12 GB RTX 4070 Ti at 480p, 5 s: about 105 s per clip, the same wall as the larryvrh Turbo LoRA at 6 steps, and on a face-visible image-to-video test the 8-step turbo was sharper than the 20-step plain beta5 at half the time, identity and dialogue held. Sampler is res_multistep / simple, the author's pick for motion quality; LCM was softer on faces in our tests. This is a separate download from the plain beta5 pack (different file); pick one unless you want both. Grafted character from LTX 2.3, Wan 2.2 and Krea 2 means their community licences apply alongside the MiniMax H3 licence. Since 1.1.0 a fourth card, Character PV: one character design sheet in, a 15-second 13-shot reveal trailer with typography cards, music and a name card out (about 4 1/2 minutes at 480p).",
  "tags": [
    "Local",
    "Video",
    "T2V",
    "MiniMax H3",
    "Finetune",
    "10Eros"
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "id": "minimax-h3-10eros-beta5-turbo-t2v",
      "name": "MiniMax H3 Text to Video (10Eros Max beta5, Turbo)",
      "icon": "🎬",
      "previewImage": "previews/minimax-h3-10eros-beta5-turbo-t2v.jpg",
      "description": "TenStrip's 10Eros Max beta5 TURBO-hybrid (INT8, 21 GB): beta5 with the turbo delta fused into the checkpoint, run on the unmodified official graph at res_multistep / simple, 8 steps. No Turbo LoRA node, no second file.\n\nTwo-seed bake-off against the plain beta5 and the original 10Eros packs (RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB, 864x480, 5 s, vanilla ComfyUI, no attention accelerators): ~105 s per clip against ~200 s for 20-step beta5; on a face-visible image-to-video test it was sharper at frame 60 than the 20-step file (589 vs 502 Laplacian) with identity held and the scripted line word-perfect. One seed put the key light in frame on a locked-off portrait; a second did not, so treat composition as seed-dependent at 8 steps.\n\nThe author's own advice: full-step audio is better than turbo audio, and keep Spectrum and step caching OFF for reference-driven shots. Free system RAM matters more than VRAM; keep 16 GB+ free.\n\nVerified in SimpliGen 1.59.1 / engine v0.34.2 on a 12 GB RTX 4070 Ti: 5 s at 864x480, 8 steps, 84 s warm with the app's Faster Attention on; the scripted line arrived word-perfect at the scripted time.",
