      "previewImage": "previews/minimax-h3-10eros-beta5-turbo-character-pv.jpg",
      "description": "CHARACTER PV: a 15-second, 13-shot character-reveal trailer with five kinetic typography cards, native music and a name-and-title card at the end, driven by ONE reference image, on the 10Eros Max beta5 TURBO-hybrid checkpoint. Same skeleton as the DaSiWa Character PV card, different look: this checkpoint reads skin, fabric and low-key light differently, and it is the one to use if the rest of your shots for that character are already on 10Eros. The method comes from Smart Bobo (机智波玩ai): make a character design sheet first (a 16:9 board with the name as title, a big full-body centre figure, FRONT/BACK/SIDE views, pose studies and detail crops - any image editor that keeps identity will do, e.g. Qwen Image 2.1 or Krea 2), put that sheet in the Reference slot, and write the prompt as the six-section H3 reference brief following the 13-shot skeleton: [Shot 1] extreme close-up mid-motion; [Shot 2] At 00:01.100 a hand gesture that emits a light trail; [Shot 3] At 00:02.200 card 1 (e.g. \"ACTIVE\"); [Shot 4] At 00:03.200 card 2 (\"MODE: ENGAGE\"); [Shot 5] At 00:04.100 whip pan into the venue; [Shot 6] At 00:05.200 low tilt up the outfit; [Shot 7] At 00:06.200 card 3 (\"SYSTEM\" / \"LINK\"); [Shot 8] At 00:06.900 a turn; [Shot 9] At 00:07.900 card 4 (\"TARGET LOCK\"); [Shot 10] At 00:08.600 a close pass by the lens; [Shot 11] At 00:09.600 the only black card (\"FULL DRIVE\"); [Shot 12] At 00:10.300 the hero pose in the venue; [Shot 13] At 00:12.300 the identity card with the NAME and a TITLE. Every card is entered and left by a gesture-triggered wipe, the character is a large crop on every card, and each shot ends with its own sound beat. Change the card strings, the name, the title and the venue to give each video its own personality; keep the timestamps. The full template with every shot spelled out: https://github.com/michaeldune/simpligen-presets/blob/master/docs/character-pv-template.md Set Duration to 15 (the skeleton needs it) and start at 480p for previews: at 15 seconds the 480p tier is the sweet spot on a 12 GB card, and pushing the resolution up smears the typography rather than sharpening it. About 4 1/2 minutes for a 15-second trailer at 480p on a 12 GB card. No dialogue support: the brief states no dialogue by design.",
